# Journee Design Governance Rules

These rules are permanent agent instructions for the Journee repository.

The canonical design authority is:

`docs/JOURNEE_MASTER_LOCK_SPEC.md`

Never override JOURNEE_MASTER_LOCK_SPEC.md unless the user explicitly requests modification of the master specification itself.

## Mandatory Agent Instructions

- Read and enforce `docs/JOURNEE_MASTER_LOCK_SPEC.md` before changing UI, layout, motion, typography, navigation, profile, homepage, imagery, or shared visual primitives.
- Treat the master spec as mandatory. It is not guidance, preference, or optional style direction.
- Preserve cinematic behavior across all Journee surfaces.
- Preserve homepage timing, including the 60000 ms hero rotation interval and the slow cross-fade transition behavior.
- Preserve atmosphere behavior, including destination-aware scene treatments and environmental layers.
- Preserve typography, including cinematic display scale, editorial hierarchy, uppercase micro-labels, and restrained sans controls.
- Preserve navigation spacing, warm hover states, glassy controls, and the "My Journee" profile affordance.
- Preserve profile behavior as a cinematic traveler profile, not a generic account portal.
- Preserve image rotation behavior and unique destination image selection.
- Prevent future UI drift by using established Journee primitives, tokens, spacing, overlays, and motion patterns.
- Prevent accidental redesigns. Do not replace established Journee screens with new visual systems unless the user explicitly requests a master spec modification.
- Prevent visible slideshow UI. Do not add carousel dots, arrows, thumbnails, slide counters, progress bars, pause/play controls, or any visible hero slideshow mechanism.
- Prevent SaaS/dashboard styling. Do not introduce generic admin dashboards, CRM shells, analytics surfaces, sterile white app layouts, or productivity-tool styling.
- Keep operational surfaces travel-native, cinematic, dark, atmospheric, image-led, and warm-accented.

## Conflict Rule

If a user request conflicts with `docs/JOURNEE_MASTER_LOCK_SPEC.md`, stop and ask whether the user wants to modify the master specification itself. Do not silently override the lock.

## Review Checklist

Before finishing any UI change, confirm:

- `docs/JOURNEE_MASTER_LOCK_SPEC.md` was followed.
- Homepage hero timing remains locked when touched.
- Cinematic background behavior remains intact when touched.
- Atmosphere layers remain destination-aware when touched.
- Typography hierarchy remains cinematic when touched.
- Navigation spacing and profile entry remain intact when touched.
- Profile behavior remains travel-native when touched.
- Image rotation remains meaningful and non-repetitive when touched.
- No visible slideshow UI was added.
- No SaaS/dashboard styling was introduced.

